--
does not uniquely resolve
--
N5008 [over.match.list], [over.ics.list], [over.ics.rank]: list-initializing a
class from a braced-init-list ranks its constructors by the element conversion
sequences; a constructor taking the elements directly (vec(int) for {7}) is
preferred over the copy/move constructor (whose ICS from {7} is a user-defined
conversion).  CBMC treats both as equally viable and reports "symbol 'vec' does
not uniquely resolve".  Same error class as the "symbol 'codet' does not
uniquely resolve" dog-food noise (std_code.h, `codet(ID_assume, {std::move(expr)})`).
Flip to CORE once brace-init overload ranking prefers the direct
element-taking constructor.
